#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:1
msgid "Feature Name: cargo_min_publish_age"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:2
msgid "Start Date: 2026-02-23"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:3
msgid ""
"RFC PR: [rust-lang/rfcs#3923](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3923)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:4
msgid ""
"Tracking Issue: [rust-lang/cargo#17009](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/"
"issues/17009)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:9
msgid ""
"This proposal adds a new configuration option to cargo allowing users to "
"specify a minimum age for dependency versions. When specified, Cargo won't "
"use a version of a registry crate that is newer than the minimum age, with a "
"way to override for exceptions like urgent security fixes."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:14
msgid "An example configuration would be:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:16 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:58
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[registry]\n"
"global-min-publish-age = \"14 days\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:21
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:24
msgid ""
"There are a couple of reasons why one may wish not to use the most recent "
"version of a package:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:26
msgid ""
"Some [supply chain attacks](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Supply_chain_attack) are found by automated scanners on newly published "
"package versions. Recent supply chain attacks on the NPM ecosystem have "
"drawn attention to the value of waiting on these automated scanners. For "
"more background on version maturity requirements as a risk mitigation, see "
"[We should all be using dependency cooldowns](https://blog.yossarian."
"net/2025/11/21/We-should-all-be-using-dependency-cooldowns) and [Dependency "
"cooldowns, redux](https://blog.yossarian.net/2025/12/13/cooldowns-redux)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:34
msgid ""
"There would be value in a gradual roll out scheme for the ecosystem. New "
"versions can introduce inadvertent breaking changes, bugs, or security "
"vulnerabilities. Having everyone discover these problems at once leads to a "
"wider, costlier disruption to the ecosystem. Some maintainers are fine being "
"on the bleeding edge, taking on those costs, and acting as a canary for the "
"ecosystem. Those who are more risk averse can choose how much stagnation "
"they are willing to accept for others to discover these problems and get "
"them worked out. Maintainers may even want to blend these in one project: "
"keep risks down for local development while CI has a dependency version "
"canary job to identify future problems and track their status. Granted, this "
"only helps if the problems are discovered by yourself or others. Any fixes "
"will also be subject to the minimum-release age but at least these will be "
"available to upgrade to so long as there is an exception mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:42
msgid ""
"Allowing maintainers to encourage a certain degree of maturity for "
"dependency versions can help these use cases."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:44
msgid ""
"Note that this is **not** a full solution to compromised dependencies. It "
"can increase the protection against certain types of \"supply chain\" "
"attacks, but not all of them. As such, using this feature should not be "
"relied upon for security by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:48
msgid "Guide-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:51
msgid ""
"The `registry.global-min-publish-age` [configuration option](https://doc."
"rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html)[^1] for Cargo can be used to "
"specify a minimum age for published versions to use. When set, Cargo treats "
"versions with a publish time (\"pubtime\") newer than that duration: Cargo "
"will not use a too-new version unless it is already recorded in `Cargo."
"lock`, and will generate an error if there are no longer any compatible "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:56
msgid "For example, in your `<repo>/.cargo/config.toml`, you may have:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:63
msgid "Running `cargo update` will look something like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:71
msgid "While a CI job runs:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:84
msgid "This will mean that:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:86
msgid ""
"Locally, `cargo update` will only select versions older than the minimum "
"publish age, e.g., `some-package@1.2.3`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:88
msgid ""
"This CI job will verify the latest versions of your dependencies, e.g., "
"`some-package@1.3.0`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:91 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:350
msgid "Per-registry configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:93
msgid ""
"It is also possible to configure the `min-publish-age` per cargo registry. "
"`registries.<name>.min-publish-age` sets the minimum publish age for the "
"`<name>` registry. And `registry.min-publish-age` sets it for crates.io."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:97
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:98
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[registries.my-org]\n"
"index = \"https://my.org\"\n"
"min-publish-age = \"0\" # this registry is fully trusted\n"
"\n"
"[registry]\n"
"# Default for any registry without a specific value\n"
"global-min-publish-age = \"14 days\"\n"
"# Value to use for crates.io\n"
"min-publish-age = \"5 days\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:110
msgid "This will use a minimum publish age of"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:111
msgid "5 days for crates.io"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:112
msgid "no minimum for `my-org`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:113
msgid "14 days for any other registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:115
msgid "When no version matches"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:117
msgid ""
"If no version of a dependency satisfies both the version requirement and the "
"minimum publish age, the resolve will error, similar to when all matching "
"versions are yanked:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:120
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo update\n"
"error: failed to select a version for the requirement `some-package = "
"\"^1.3\"`\n"
"  version 1.3.0 is too new (published 2 days ago, minimum age 14 days)\n"
"help: to preserve the min-publish-age, downgrade the version requirement to "
"`\"1.1\"`\n"
"help: to use `\"1.3\"` anyways, re-resolve with "
"`CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_PUBLISH_AGE=allow`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:128
msgid "Using newer versions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:130
msgid ""
"In some cases, it may be desirable to use a version that is newer than the "
"minimum publish age. For example, `some-package` from [earlier](#guide-level-"
"explanation) has a fix for a vulnerability in v1.3.0."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:133
msgid ""
"The `CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_PUBLISH_AGE=allow` environment variable can "
"temporarily disable the check:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:143
msgid ""
"Once the versions are recorded in `Cargo.lock`, subsequent resolves will "
"keep them."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:146
msgid "As specified in `.cargo/config.toml` files"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:148
msgid "Reference-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:151
msgid ""
"This RFC adds a few new configuration options to [cargo configuration]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:153
msgid ""
"Added to [Configuration Format](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/"
"config.html#configuration-format)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:155
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[resolver]\n"
"incompatible-publish-age = \"deny\" # Specifies how resolver reacts to "
"these\n"
"\n"
"[registries.<name>]\n"
"min-publish-age = \"...\"  # Override `registry.global-min-publish-age` for "
"this registry\n"
"\n"
"[registry]\n"
"min-publish-age = \"...\"  # Override `registry.global-min-publish-age` for "
"crates.io\n"
"global-min-publish-age = \"0\"  # Minimum time span allowed for packages "
"from this registry\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:167
msgid ""
"Added to [`[resolver]`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config."
"html#resolver)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:169
msgid "`resolver.incompatible-publish-age`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:171 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:186
#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:203 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:218
msgid "Type: String"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:172
msgid "Default: `\"deny\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:173
msgid "Environment: `CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_PUBLISH_AGE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:175
msgid ""
"When resolving the version of a dependency, specify the behavior for "
"versions with a `pubtime` (if present) that is incompatible with `registry."
"min-publish-age`. Values include:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:177
msgid "`allow`: treat pubtime-incompatible versions like any other version"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:178
msgid ""
"`deny`: ignore pubtime-incompatible versions unless they already exist in "
"the lock file"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:180
msgid "See the resolver chapter for more details."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:182
msgid ""
"Added to [`[registries]`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config."
"html#registries)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:184
msgid "`registries.min-publish-age`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:187 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:204
msgid "Default: none"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:188
msgid "Environment: `CARGO_REGISTRIES_<name>_MIN_PUBLISH_AGE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:190
msgid ""
"Specifies the minimum timespan since a version's `pubtime` that it may be "
"considered for `resolver.incompatible-publish-age` for packages from this "
"registry. If not set, `registry.global-min-publish-age` will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:192
msgid "Will be ignored if the registry does not support this."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:194 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:209
#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:224
msgid "It supports the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:196 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:211
#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:226 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:485
msgid ""
"An integer followed by “seconds”, “minutes”, “hours”, “days”, “weeks”, or "
"“months”"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:197 src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:212
#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:227
msgid "`\"0\"` to allow all packages"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:199
msgid ""
"Added to [`[registry]`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config."
"html#registry)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:201
msgid "`registry.min-publish-age`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:205
msgid "Environment: `CARGO_REGISTRY_MIN_PUBLISH_AGE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:207
msgid ""
"Specifies the minimum timespan since a version's `pubtime` that it may be "
"considered for `resolver.incompatible-publish-age` for packages from crates."
"io. If not set, `registry.global-min-publish-age` will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:214
msgid "Generally, `\"0\"`, `\"N days\"`, and `\"N weeks\"` will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:216
msgid "`registry.global-min-publish-age`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:219
msgid "Default: `\"0\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:220
msgid "Environment: `CARGO_REGISTRY_GLOBAL_MIN_PUBLISH_AGE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:222
msgid ""
"Specifies the global minimum timespan since a version's `pubtime` that it "
"may be considered for `resolver.incompatible-publish-age` for packages. If "
"`min-publish-age` is not set for a specific registry using `registries."
"<name>.min-publish-age`, Cargo will use this minimum publish age."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:229
msgid ""
"Added to [Resolver](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/resolver.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:231
msgid ""
"_\"Pubtime-incompatible versions\" as a sibling section to [Yanked versions]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/resolver.html#yanked-versions)_"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:233
msgid ""
"Versions with a publish time newer than the configured [`min-publish-age`]"
"(config.md#registryglobal-min-publish-age) are considered pubtime-"
"incompatible. When [`resolver.incompatible-publish-age`](config."
"md#resolverincompatible-publish-age) is set to `deny`, the resolver will "
"ignore these versions unless they already exist in the `Cargo.lock` file. "
"Setting the config to `allow` would disable the check, which if combined "
"with `cargo update --precise`, cargo would pull in a specific version and "
"its transitive dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:246
msgid "Applicability"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:248
msgid ""
"The minimum publish age check applies to the following dependency sources:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:250
msgid ""
"Dependencies fetched from a registry that publishes `pubtime`, such as "
"crates.io."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:251
msgid ""
"Does not apply to git or path dependencies, in part because there is not "
"always an obvious publish time, or a way to find alternative versions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:254
msgid ""
"Does not apply to registries that don't set `pubtime`, as there is no "
"reliable way to know when the version was published."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:256
msgid ""
"For [source replacement](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/source-"
"replacement.html), registry mirrors are expected to preserve `pubtime` from "
"the index to be applicable. Local registries and directory (vendored) "
"sources typically don't have `pubtime`, so the check does not apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:260
msgid ""
"`cargo install` is subject to `min-publish-age` and will not select pubtime-"
"incompatible versions. `resolver.incompatible-publish-age` cannot override "
"this as the `[resolver]` table does not apply to `cargo install`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:265
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:268
msgid "Slower problem discovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:270
msgid ""
"The biggest drawback is that if this is widely used, it could potentially "
"lead to it taking longer for problems to be discovered after a version is "
"published. However, most likely, there will be a spread of values used, "
"depending on risk tolerance, and hopefully the result is actually that there "
"will be a more gradual rollout in most cases."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:274
msgid ""
"Also, even if all users of a crate set a minimum publish age there is still "
"value in a delay, because it provides time for automated security scanners, "
"and human reviewers to review the changes before the new version is pulled "
"in by updates. And in the case of a malicious release made using compromised "
"credentials, it gives the actual developer time to realize their credentials "
"have been compromised and yank the version before it is widely used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:278
msgid ""
"On a related note, delayed discovery might make authors feel it is \"too "
"late\" to yank because wall-clock time has passed. However, the minimum "
"publish age also means most consumers haven't resolved the new version yet, "
"so a yank remains low-disruption for longer than elapsed time alone would "
"suggest. The practical yank window is shaped more by adoption than by the "
"calendar."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:285
msgid "Disjoint resolver config values"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:287
msgid ""
"`resolver.incompatible-publish-age` supports `allow`/`deny` while `resolver."
"incompatible-rust-versions` supports `allow`/`fallback`, which may be "
"confusing. See [Starting with `deny`](#starting-with-deny) for why the value "
"sets differ."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:292
msgid "Rationale and Alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:295
msgid "Configuration Locations"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:297
msgid ""
"The locations and names of the configuration options in this proposal were "
"chosen to be consistent with existing Cargo options, as described in "
"[Related Options in Cargo](#related-options)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:300
msgid "Configuration Names"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:302
msgid ""
"The term \"publish\" was used rather than \"package\", \"version\", or "
"\"release\" to make it clear that this only applies to crates that are "
"published in a registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:305
msgid ""
"`publish` is redundant with this being in the `registry` table. This helps "
"with the above disambiguation and for clarity in discussing this as a "
"shorthand."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:308
msgid ""
"`cooldown` was avoided due to the term generally referring to throttling "
"while we are looking for a certain maturity."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:310
msgid "Starting with `deny`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:312
msgid "`resolver.incompatible-publish-age` starts with `allow` and `deny`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:314
msgid ""
"Unlike `resolver.incompatible-rust-versions` which starts with `fallback`, "
"`deny` is viable here because `pubtime` data is exhaustive. crates.io sets "
"it for every version once backfilled, so there are no gaps that would cause "
"spurious errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:319
msgid ""
"A `fallback` option would deprioritize too-new versions but still allow them "
"as a last resort. This is deferred because it opens the yank attack vector: "
"a malicious actor with the right permissions could publish a malicious "
"version and yank the safe versions. It then forces the resolver to fall back "
"to the malicious too-new version. `deny` prevents this by erroring instead "
"of falling back."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:325
msgid ""
"`fallback` may be useful in the future for risk-tolerant workflows that "
"prefer a degraded resolve over an error, particularly when combined with "
"other tools that validate pubtime-incompatible versions. It would also help "
"with `cargo update --precise` for packages with transitive dependencies. For "
"example, `CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_PUBLISH_AGE=fallback cargo update clap "
"--precise 4.5.3` would pull in only the necessary too-new transitive "
"dependencies rather than disabling the check entirely with `allow`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:334
msgid "Timestamp vs duration"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:336
msgid "Some prior art:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:337
msgid "exclusively use a timestamp"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:338
msgid "allow either a timestamp or a relative time within the same field"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:340
msgid ""
"While a timestamp has its uses (see [`--publish-time`](https://doc.rust-lang."
"org/cargo/reference/unstable.html#lockfile-publish-time)), it wouldn't be as "
"ergonomic for this use case."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:344
msgid ""
"Designing the field to support both would create a trap for users trying to "
"reproduce a problem from the past in that they are likely to set the "
"timestamp but overlook that they need to take the existing duration into "
"account. Even if they do remember to take the existing duration into "
"account, it would be more convenient if they can be set separately."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:348
msgid "Setting the timestamp to resolve to is left as a future possibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:352
msgid ""
"Allowing the minimum age to be configurable per registry provides a simple "
"mechanism to use different minimum ages for different sets of packages, "
"including possibly no minimum in common situations such as using an internal "
"registry where the crates are completely trusted."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:357
msgid ""
"This makes it less necessary to have more complicated configuration for "
"rules for including and excluding sets of packages from the age policy, or "
"setting different age policies for different packages."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:361
msgid "Exclude list"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:363
msgid "Exclude lists tend to be used either for:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:364
msgid ""
"Forcing a specific newer version: we have this covered through "
"`CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_PUBLISH_AGE=allow` combined with `cargo update "
"--precise`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:365
msgid ""
"Marking a source as always trusted: we have this covered through per-"
"registry configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:367
msgid ""
"One problem with an exclude list is that they tend to be a static solution "
"(all versions) for a transient problem (a subset of versions). This can "
"leave people open to an attack after a high-value upgrade. An exclude list "
"of just names is helpful for \"I have a trusted package source\" scenario, "
"but less so for \"I need a security fix now\". The user must remember to "
"remove the exclusion once it is no longer needed, or they lose protection "
"for future versions of that package. We could make the exclude list use the "
"[Package ID Spec](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/pkgid-spec.html) "
"format and even require a full version to be specified."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:375
msgid ""
"Users likely will need to exclude transitive dependencies as well. For "
"instance, to use a too-new version of `clap`, you may also need to exclude "
"`clap_builder`, `clap_derive`, and `clap_lex`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:378
msgid ""
"An exclude list can always be added in the future if a strong enough use "
"case presents itself. By delaying, we can also take into account any future "
"changes. For example, if the focus is on different levels of trust within "
"the same registry, we could design a solution around [registry namespacing]"
"(https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/survey-of-organizational-ownership-and-"
"registry-namespace-designs-for-cargo-and-crates-io/24027/4), assuming "
"support is added."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:384
msgid "Using Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock (i.e. \"do nothing\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:386
msgid ""
"You can pin versions in your `Cargo.toml` but that is a manual process and "
"doesn't cover transitive dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:389
msgid ""
"Users can manage all of their direct and transitive dependencies in a `Cargo."
"lock` file but that is tedious and it is easy to overlook new entries on "
"implicit lockfile changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:391
msgid "Why not leave this to third party tools?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:393
msgid ""
"There are already some third party tools that fulfill this functionality to "
"some degree. For example, dependabot and renovate can be used for updating "
"Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock, and both support some form of minimum publish "
"age. And the cargo-cooldown project provides an alternative to `cargo "
"update` that respects a minimum publish age."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:397
msgid ""
"However, these tools only work for updating and adding dependencies outside "
"of cargo itself, they do not have any impact on local changes, like directly "
"editing `Cargo.toml` causing an implicit `Cargo.lock` update, `cargo "
"update`, or `cargo add`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:400
msgid "Prior Art"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:403
msgid ""
"[\"Package Managers Need to Cool Down\"](https://nesbitt.io/2026/03/04/"
"package-managers-need-to-cool-down.html) discusses several implementations "
"of this in various package managers (including this RFC)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:406
msgid ""
"[\"Dependency-cooldown discussions warm up\"](https://lwn.net/"
"Articles/1068692/) covers the broader ecosystem debate around dependency "
"cooldowns, including an alternative \"upload queue\" approach where "
"registries delay distribution rather than consumers delay adoption."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:411
msgid "Debian \"testing\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:413
msgid ""
"Debian's \"testing\" distribution consists of packages from unstable that "
"have been in the \"unstable\" distribution for a certain minimum age (2-10 "
"days depending on an `urgency` field in the package changelog), have been "
"built for all previously supported targets, have their dependencies in "
"testing, and don't have any new release-critical bugs."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:415
msgid ""
"Users of \"unstable\" include early adopters who don't mind being the canary "
"when things break (and reporting the aforementioned bugs, release-critical "
"or otherwise). Users of \"testing\" get slightly older packages and a "
"reduced chance of release-critical bugs."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:417
msgid "pnpm"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:419
msgid ""
"`minimumReleaseAge` is a configuration option which takes a number of "
"minutes as an argument. It then won't update or install releases that were "
"released less than that many minutes ago. This also applies to transitive "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:421
msgid ""
"`minimumReleaseAgeExclude` is an array of package names, or package patterns "
"for which the `minimumReleaseAge` does not apply, and the newest applicable "
"release is always used. It also allows specifying specific versions to be "
"allowed."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:423
msgid ""
"Both configuration options can be set in global config, a project-specific "
"config file, or with environment variables (for a specific invocation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:425
msgid "yarn"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:427
msgid ""
"Has a configuration setting that can be used in `.yarnrc.yml` named "
"`npmMinimalAgeGate` that can be used to set the minimum age for installed "
"package releases. It looks like it allows specifying units, as the example "
"for three days is `3d`, however I haven't found any definitive description "
"of the syntax."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:429
msgid ""
"As far as I can tell, there is no way to provide exclusions to this rule, or "
"different times for different packages or repositories."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:431
msgid "uv"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:433
msgid ""
"The `--exclude-newer` option can be used to set a timestamp (using RFC 3339 "
"format), or a duration (either \"friendly\" or ISO 8601 format) and won't "
"use releases that happened after that timestamp. There is also an `--exclude-"
"newer-package` option, which allows overriding the `exclude-newer` time for "
"individual packages."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:436
msgid ""
"Both of these settings can also be used in the `uv` configuration file "
"(`pyproject.toml`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:438
msgid "pip"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:440
msgid ""
"Pip has an `--uploaded-prior-to` option that only uses versions that were "
"uploaded prior to an ISO 8601 timestamp. Can also be controlled with the "
"`PIP_UPLOADED_PRIOR_TO` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:443
msgid "dependabot"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:445
msgid "The `cooldown` option provides a number of settings, including:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:447
msgid "`default-days` – Default minimum age of release, in days"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:448
msgid ""
"`semver-major-days`, `semver-minor-days`, `semver-patch-days` -- Override "
"the cooldown/minimum-release-age based on what kind of release it is."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:449
msgid ""
"`include` / `exclude` – a list of packages to include/exclude in the "
"\"cooldown\". Supports wildcards. `exclude` has higher priority than "
"`include`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:451
msgid "\"Security\" updates bypass the `cooldown` settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:453
msgid "Dependabot doesn't support cooldown for all package managers."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:455
msgid "This is specified in the dependabot configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:457
msgid "renovate"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:459
msgid ""
"The options below can be provided in global, or project-specific "
"configuration files, as a CLI option, or as an environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:461
msgid ""
"`minimumReleaseAge` specifies a duration which all updates must be older "
"than for renovate to create an update. It looks like the duration "
"specification uses units (ex. \"3 days\"), however, again I can't find a "
"precise specification for the syntax."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:463
msgid ""
"It is possible to create separate rules with different `minimumReleaseAge` "
"configurations, on a per-package basis, or across groups of packages/"
"registries."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:465
msgid "\"Security\" updates bypass the minimum release age checks."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:467
msgid "deno"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:469
msgid ""
"Deno supports a [configuration option](https://deno.com/blog/"
"v2.6#controlling-dependency-stability) for `minimumDependencyAge` in the "
"configuration file, or `--minimum-dependency-age` on the CLI. It supports an "
"ISO-8601 duration, RFC 3339 timestamp, or an integer of minutes."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:472
msgid "cargo-cooldown"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:474
msgid ""
"There is an existing experimental third-party crate that provides a plugin "
"for enforcing a cooldown: \\[https://github.com/dertin/cargo-cooldown\\]"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:476
msgid "Related Options in Cargo"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:479
msgid "Some precedents in Cargo"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:481
msgid ""
"[`cache.auto-clean-frequency`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/"
"config.html#cacheauto-clean-frequency)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:483
msgid "\"never\" — Never deletes old files."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:484
msgid "\"always\" — Checks to delete old files every time Cargo runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:488
msgid ""
"[`resolver.incompatible-rust-versions`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/"
"reference/config.html#resolverincompatible-rust-versions)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:490
msgid ""
"Controls behavior in relation to your [`package.rust-version`](https://doc."
"rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/rust-version.html) and those set by potential "
"dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:492
msgid "Values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:494
msgid "allow: treat rust-version-incompatible versions like any other version"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:495
msgid ""
"fallback: only consider rust-version-incompatible versions if no other "
"version matched"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:498
msgid ""
"[`package.resolver`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/resolver."
"html#resolver-versions) is only a version number. When adding `incompatible-"
"rust-version`, we intentionally deferred anything being done in manifests."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:500
msgid ""
"[`[registry]`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config."
"html#registry)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:502
msgid "Set default registry"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:503
msgid "Sets credential providers for all registries"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:504
msgid "Sets crates.io values"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:506
msgid ""
"[`[registries]`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config."
"html#registries)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:508
msgid "Sets registry specific values"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:510
msgid ""
"`yanked`: can't do new resolves to it but left in if already there. `--"
"precise` can force it but that doesn't apply recursively."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:512
msgid ""
"pre-release: requires opt-in through version requirement. Unstable support "
"to force it with `--precise` but that doesn't apply recursively."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:514
msgid "Unresolved Questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:517
msgid ""
"Can we, and should we, make any guarantees about security when using this "
"feature, such as \"a malicious version of a crate will not compromise the "
"build if published within the minimum publish age window\"?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:520
msgid "How do we make it clear when things are held back?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:521
msgid ""
"The \"locking\" message for [Cargo time machine (generate lock files based "
"on old registry state) #5221](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/"
"issues/5221) lists one time but the time here is dependent on where any "
"given package is from"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:522
msgid ""
"We list MSRVs for unselected packages, should we also list publish times? "
"I'm assuming that should be in local time"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:523
msgid ""
"Locking message for [Cargo time machine (generate lock files based on old "
"registry state) #5221](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/issues/5221) is in "
"UTC time, see [Tracking Issue for _lockfile-publish-time_ #16271](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/cargo/issues/16271), when relative time differences "
"likely make local time more relevant"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:524
msgid ""
"Implementation wise, will there be much complexity in getting per registry "
"information into `VersionPreferences` and using it?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:525
msgid "`deny` precedence between this and `incompatible-rust-version`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:526
msgid ""
"Both produce errors, but `incompatible-rust-version` will likely be "
"evaluated first to increase the chance of builds succeeding."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:528
msgid "Future Possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:531
msgid ""
"Support `fallback` for `resolver.incompatible-publish-age` (see [Starting "
"with `deny`](#starting-with-deny) for why this is deferred)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:533
msgid ""
"Add an exclude list for `min-publish-age` (see [Exclude list](#exclude-list) "
"for why this is deferred)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:535
msgid ""
"When all compatible older-than-min-age versions are yanked and a newer non-"
"yanked version exists, Cargo could alert the user that they may want to "
"override with `--precise`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:538
msgid ""
"Potentially support other source of publish time besides the `pubtime` field "
"from a cargo registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/3923-cargo-min-publish-age.md:539
msgid ""
"A `resolver.now` field for setting the reference time that `min-publish-age` "
"is compared against. This could be useful for offline workflows where wall-"
"clock time keeps advancing but the registry index may be stale."
msgstr ""
